# NewUnera — Admin Web App Pages (UNERA Admin + UNERA Stablecoin Admin)

**Canonical reference:** [`NewUnera/USAdmin/dashboard.html`](NewUnera/USAdmin/dashboard.html)  
All other admin pages must match it in structure, tokens, icons, and accessibility. All [new-brand-output.mdc](new-brand-output.mdc) and [newunera-color-system.mdc](newunera-color-system.mdc) rules apply in full — the sections below extend them for admin-specific patterns.

---

## 1. Output & File Naming

- **UNERA Admin** pages live in `NewUnera/UneraAdmin/` — named `login.html`, `dashboard.html`, `hc-management.html`, `hc-edit.html`; future pages: `user-management.html`, `kyc-management.html`
- **UNERA Stablecoin Admin** pages live in `NewUnera/USAdmin/` — named `login.html`, `dashboard.html`, `issuance.html`, `por.html`
- `hc-*.html` pages are **UneraAdmin-only** (consumer-side HC content management)
- `issuance.html` and `por.html` are **USAdmin-only** (stablecoin treasury operations)
- Each folder has its own `login.html` and `dashboard.html`
- Never modify or overwrite production consumer pages (`dashboard-enhanced.html`, `wallet-enhanced.html`, etc.)

---

## 2. Admin-Only CSS Tokens

Add these tokens to `:root` **after** the standard V2 token block (copy from `USAdmin/dashboard.html`):

```css
:root {
    /* Admin nav — black chrome, distinct from consumer deep-blue nav */
    --op-nav:                  var(--brand-black);    /* #000000 */

    /* Admin accent — --brand-purple as the portal differentiator */
    --op-accent:               var(--brand-purple);   /* #6a5770 */
    --op-accent-ink:           var(--brand-white);

    /* Surface tints — 10% purple matches #f0eef1 brand swatch */
    --surface-operator:        color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-purple) 10%, var(--brand-white));
    --surface-operator-strong: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-purple) 18%, var(--brand-white));
    --op-icon-well:            color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand-purple) 16%, var(--brand-white));
}
```

**Admin color logic:**
- **`--op-nav` (black `#000000`)** — nav chrome and primary action card; creates hard authority contrast vs the consumer deep-blue nav
- **`--op-accent` (purple `#6a5770`)** — login button, tab underline, card hover borders, icon wells
- **`--brand-cloud-blue` (`#ebfcf5`)** — op-pill background, alert banner surface, badge-success background, tab-badge background
- **`--surface-operator` (~`#f0eef1`)** — body wash, table headers, dropdown headers, mobile tab hover

Use `--surface-operator` for the body background, dropdown header, table header, mobile tab hover, and skeleton rows — it creates a subtle purple wash that visually distinguishes the admin apps from the consumer app without breaking the V2 brand.

