## 5. Stat Cards & Icon Wells

Stat icon wells use `--op-icon-well` (purple-tint) instead of the consumer's deep-blue tint:

```css
.stat-icon {
    background: var(--op-icon-well);   /* color-mix(purple 16%, white) */
    color: var(--brand-deep-blue);     /* deep-blue icon ink — 10.4:1 on purple-tinted well */
}
```

Positive stat changes: `color: var(--fin-up)`. Negative: `color: var(--fin-down)`. Neutral notes: `color: var(--text-secondary)`.  
Stat values: `font-size: var(--font-stat-size)` (2.5rem), `font-weight: 700`, `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.

---

## 6. Quick Action Cards

Secondary cards: `background: var(--surface-action)`, `color: var(--brand-deep-blue)` icon ink, `--op-icon-well` or `--surface-operator` icon chip background.

Primary CTA card (e.g. "Review HC Applications"): uses **black** (`--op-nav`) — matches the nav chrome for strong visual authority:

```css
.action-card.primary                   { background: var(--op-nav); color: white;
                                         box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3); }
.action-card.primary:hover             { box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); }
.action-card.primary .action-card-icon { background: var(--brand-white); }
.action-card.primary .action-card-icon svg { fill: var(--brand-black); }
```

The SVG inside the white chip uses `fill: var(--brand-black)` — black on white chip on black card; the white chip provides the visual break.

Secondary cards on hover: `border-color: var(--op-accent)` — purple hover border is consistent with the admin accent.

---

## 7. Badges (Admin Context)

In the admin apps, status badges use the **purple accent family** rather than the financial `--fin-up` green. This is an administrative portal — completion/success here is an admin workflow outcome, not a P&L signal.

```css
.badge-success {
    background: var(--brand-cloud-blue);   /* #ebfcf5 — cloud-blue tint */
    color: var(--brand-deep-blue);         /* #173d47 — passes 9:1+ on cloud-blue */
}
.badge-warning { background: var(--surface-warning-soft); color: var(--brand-deep-blue); }
.badge-error   { background: var(--error-bg); color: var(--error); }
.badge-info    { background: var(--surface-sky); color: var(--brand-deep-blue); }
```

**Rule:** Do not use `--fin-up` (`#1a7a5e`) for admin status badges — that hue is reserved for financial P&L positive figures. Use `--brand-cloud-blue` background with `--brand-deep-blue` text for admin workflow completion states.

