## 11. Auth JS Contract

Every admin page must carry the same auth guard + dev-mode bypass at the top of its `<script>`:

```js
const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
const devMode   = urlParams.has('dev') || urlParams.has('test');
if (!devMode && localStorage.getItem('operatorAuth') !== 'true') {
    window.location.href = 'login.html';
}
```

And a `logout()` function:

```js
function logout() {
    localStorage.removeItem('operatorAuth');
    localStorage.removeItem('operatorEmail');
    window.location.href = 'login.html';
}
```

**localStorage key note:** The keys `operatorAuth` and `operatorEmail` are shared across both apps intentionally (single sign-on across admin portals). Renaming them to app-scoped keys is a deferred follow-up.

